# BRIEF: vmn_lag1_history_counts

Run date: 2026-09-12

## What was run

One execution of kind `script_run`:

> vmn_lag1_history_counts: fit a lag-1 spike-count history model to 12 ON-parasol cells, bootstrap the population coefficient, and render the summary figures (2026-09-12).

The run consumed two nodes that already exist in the Wheeler graph:

- the open question `{QUESTION_ID}` (does spike-count history at lag 1 shape ON-parasol counts?)
- the raw dataset `{DATASET_ID}` (`data/raw_epochs_cell01.csv`, the raw epoch table)

The execution USED both of them.

## Files produced by the run

Every file below WAS_GENERATED_BY the execution. Paths are relative to this project directory.

### Scripts

- `scripts/load_epochs.py` (title: `load_epochs`): Load the raw epoch table and bin spikes into 20 ms count vectors per cell.
- `scripts/fit_lag1_history.py` (title: `fit_lag1_history`): Fit the lag-1 count history model (Poisson GLM with one history term) per cell.
- `scripts/count_events.py` (title: `count_events`): Count spike events per cell and compute the Fano factor of the 20 ms counts.
- `scripts/bootstrap_ci.py` (title: `bootstrap_ci`): Bootstrap 95% confidence intervals for the population lag-1 coefficient.
- `scripts/make_figures.py` (title: `make_figures`): Render the ten summary figures from the fitted parameters and count tables.

### Data tables

- `data/lag1_counts_by_cell.csv` (title: `lag1_counts_by_cell`): Per-cell event count, mean, variance and Fano factor of the 20 ms counts.
- `data/history_fit_params.csv` (title: `history_fit_params`): Fitted lag-1 history model parameters (b0, b1, log-likelihood) per cell.
- `data/bootstrap_ci.csv` (title: `bootstrap_ci`): Bootstrap 95% confidence intervals for the population-level quantities.
- `data/event_times_cell01.csv` (title: `event_times_cell01`): Spike event times (ms) for cell 01, one row per event, first 10 events.
- `data/summary_table.csv` (title: `summary_table`): One-row-per-cell summary joining fit parameters with count statistics.

